<SizeGuide
  title="Levi's Size Guide — Are Levi's True to Size? (Charts & Tips) | Attirel"
  description="Levi's jeans are true to size in modern stretch fits, but rigid and shrink-to-fit styles need sizing up. Full Levi's waist/inseam charts and fit-by-fit tips."
  brand="Levi's"
  verdictQuestion="Are Levi's true to size?"
  charts={charts}
>
  <Fragment slot="verdict">
    <strong>Mostly yes — modern stretch Levi's fit true to your actual waist measurement.</strong>
    The exceptions are the classics: rigid, non-stretch denim (and especially 501
    Shrink-to-Fit) runs tight and shrinks further, so size the waist up. Levi's sizes by real
    inches — measure your natural waist and you're most of the way there.
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="tips">
    <li><strong>501 Shrink-to-Fit:</strong> buy 1" up in the waist and 3" longer in the leg — the raw denim shrinks that much after the first washes.</li>
    <li><strong>Rigid / vintage re-issues:</strong> no stretch means no forgiveness — if between sizes, go up.</li>
    <li><strong>Stretch fits (311, 312, 511 Flex, 721):</strong> relax up to half a size with wear — if between sizes, go down.</li>
    <li><strong>W = waist in inches, L = inseam in inches</strong> — a 32×32 is a 32" waist with a 32" inseam. Measure a well-fitting pair to find your true numbers.</li>
    <li><strong>Vanity check:</strong> many people wear jeans labelled 2–3" smaller than their actual waist measurement in other brands — trust the tape, not the label you're used to.</li>
  </Fragment>
</SizeGuide>
